# 할아버지: gruff, few words, always fishing, always an excuse. (format: js/core/villagers.js)

=== person haraboji
at morning gang 64 60
at afternoon gang 64 60
at evening gang 64 60
greet hb_hi
chat 0 hb_fish
chat 0 hb_know
chat 0 hb_busy
ask 할머니 hb_ask_gm
ask 물고기 hb_ask_fish
bye hb_bye

=== scene hb_hi
haraboji: ...{네}.
(He nods without taking his eyes off the water. From him, that is a warm welcome.)

=== scene hb_fish
haraboji: {물고기}{가|이/가} {없어요}.
(He stares at his float, which has not moved.)
* {물고기} {있어요}! -> hb_fish_a
* {네}, {없어요}. -> hb_fish_b

=== scene hb_fish_a
haraboji[surprised]: {어디}? {어디}?!
(You point at a ripple. It was the wind.)
haraboji[happy]: 하하. {없어요}.
(He almost smiles. Almost.)
! rel haraboji +1

=== scene hb_fish_b
haraboji: {네}. {없어요}.
(A long, comfortable silence.)

=== scene hb_know
haraboji: {학생}{은|은/는} {낚시} {알아요}?
(He holds the rod out an inch in your direction.)
* {네}, {알아요}. -> hb_know_a
* {아니요}, {몰라요}. -> hb_know_b

=== scene hb_know_a
haraboji: {정말}?
(He hands you the rod. Within ten seconds the line is wrapped around a reed.)
haraboji[happy]: 하하하. {몰라요}!

=== scene hb_know_b
haraboji[happy]: {괜찮아요}. {저}{도} {몰라요}. 하하.
(He lifts his empty bucket to prove it.)
! rel haraboji +1

=== scene hb_busy
haraboji: {오늘}{은|은/는} {바빠요}.
(He has not moved in an hour.)
* {바빠요}? -> hb_busy_a
* [Sit down next to him] -> hb_busy_b

=== scene hb_busy_a
haraboji: {네}. {낚시}{하거든요|거든요}.
(He says it with a perfectly straight face.)

=== scene hb_busy_b
~ You sit down on the next rock. The river goes by. Nobody says anything for a while.
haraboji: ...{좋아요}.
(He keeps his eyes on the float.)
! rel haraboji +1

=== scene hb_bye
haraboji: ...{낚시}{하거든요|거든요}.
(He is busy. He has always been busy.)

=== scene hb_ask_gm
haraboji: ...
(He doesn't answer for a long time. The float bobs.)
haraboji[sad]: {좋은} {친구}{예요|이에요}. {옛날}{부터}.
(Since long ago. He says nothing more, and you don't ask.)
! rel haraboji +1

=== scene hb_ask_fish
haraboji[happy]: {물고기}? {큰} {물고기}{가|이/가} {있어요}. {여기}.
(He points at a dark patch of water under the bridge. One day.)